      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Applying warm compresses is a safe and recommended home remedy to help encourage natural drainage and relieve discomfort. Soak a clean washcloth in warm (not hot) water and apply it to the area for 10 to 15 minutes several times a day. Over-the-counter pain relievers, like ibuprofen, may also help manage the pain while your body works to resolve the bump. Keep the area clean, and watch for signs of worsening infection like increasing redness, swelling, or fever.",
